  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Wyoming federal contract obligations totaled $520M in FY2026 to date. Award count reached 2,050 and average award size was $254K. Obligations were up 4.7% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show obligations of $390M in FY21, $559M in FY22, $470M in FY23, $532M in FY24, and $497M in FY25. The Department of the Interior led buying in FY2026 to date with $312M, followed by the Department of Defense with $80M and the Department of Veterans Affairs with $41.3M. RECORD STEEL AND CONSTRUCTION, INC. received $129M and G.S.E. CONSTRUCTION COMPANY, INC. received $109M in FY2026 to date. Water and Sewer Line and Related Structures Construction was the largest industry by obligations with $246M, followed by Highway, Street, and Bridge Construction with $62.6M and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction with $57.1M. The note on reporting clarifies that all figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial. Use these figures for planning, compliance, and market outreach efforts in Wyoming government contracting.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies drove federal spending in Wyoming in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of the Interior obligated $312M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $80M and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $41.3M. The Department of Transportation obligated $39.2M and the General Services Administration obligated $26.7M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who captured the largest shares of Wyoming federal contracting dollars?",
        "body": "RECORD STEEL AND CONSTRUCTION, INC. received $129M and G.S.E. CONSTRUCTION COMPANY, INC. received $109M in FY2026 to date. THE ARMORED GROUP LLC received $26.4M and AECOM + TETRA TECH JOINT VENTURE received $22.7M. Water and Sewer Line and Related Structures Construction led industries with $246M, followed by Highway, Street, and Bridge Construction with $62.6M."
      }
    ]
  },
